p.src:
Schematically, the revision process looks like $\begin{aligned}
\text{draft} &\to \text{imagined reader}, \\
\text{draft} + \text{actual reader response} &\to \text{revision}.\end{aligned}$ The first arrow is necessary. The second is what saves us.

